WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.280
 It's not uncommon 
  for us to teach the same course, 

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.640
 but maybe with a few slight modifications.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:12.800
 Rather than creating the same course 
  multiple times, we can actually reuse 

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.680
 our RStudio Cloud workspace 
  using one of two methods. 

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.440
 We can remove all of our learners 
  once the course is completed 

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.320
 and reuse the workspace.  

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.680
 Or we can copy the workspace 
  for a new cohort of learners. 

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.720
 To reuse our existing workspace 
  by removing learners 

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:32.400
 we can go to the members 
  tab located at the top of our workspace. 

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:37.920
 From here, we can navigate to a specific 
  member and click the delete icon here. 

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.040
 We can repeat this for any 
  and all members in our workspace. 

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:46.040
 However, if we'd like to remove 
  large numbers of learners, we'll need 

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.880
 to use the rscloud package. 

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:53.240
 It's also important to 
  note that only admins can remove learners. 

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:57.360
 This means that if you'd like any 
  of your co-instructors or teaching assistants 

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.760
 to help remove members 
  from the shared workspace, 

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.880
 they'll need to have their membership 
  roles switch to administrator. 

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.760
 Rather than remove learners, 
  we can copy our workspace. 

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.600
 Copying our workspace 
  allows us to take all of the existing 

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.760
 shared files to a new workspace 
  where we will be the only member. 

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.560
 Just note that any private files 
  in our workspace will not be copied over. 

